### Scope (9 cherry-picked M2 commits b6d7dbe..c580388 + close-out cdd798f + format e2e7384 + ledger df23f19)
- Chat/message CRUD + library/chat CRUD over the Product Wire (29 ops, 1:1 kernel dispatch);
- provider configs with secrets OUT of the DB (`secret_ref` only, fail-closed `SECRET_UNAVAILABLE` without a SecretStore);
- OpenAI-compatible production provider (api key ONLY in the `Authorization: Bearer` header; errors carry codes/params only);
- prompt pipeline in the Kernel: history/character/persona/lorebook/instruct/token budget → immutable `PromptPlan` stored durably (`prompt_plans`, migration 5);
- durable `GenerationRun`/`GenerationStep` journal (migration 6) with CAS transitions, `WaitingForTool` as a durable wait, tool-call loop (`MAX_TOOL_CALLS=8`), idempotency keys, crash-at-wait reopen+resume, stale tool-result rejection;
- streaming/cancel/retry + durable save (terminal writers commit message + status atomically);
- packaged golden slice on the Desktop host — `NEOTA_DESKTOP_SMOKE=1` kernel-flow smoke (real Tauri IPC path);
- ADR-0044 (generation run/step/tool model, ТЗ §19.2 #6) + companion docs + capability matrix 27 rows.

### Honest scope boundaries (not defects)
1. Plugin interceptors NOT in the PromptPlan (`plain-messages-v1` only);
2. `response_reserved=0` heuristic token estimator (exact tokenizer profiles later);
3. interrupted runs = explicit recoverable terminal state (resume = UI/user retry, ТЗ §8.3 branch);
4. synchronous writer thread + mpsc backpressure (`EmitStatus::Stop` at step boundaries).
Unsupported inputs surface typed `UnsupportedError` (`CAPABILITY_UNAVAILABLE`) — never a silent legacy downgrade (wireBridge.ts).

